From 173458290f3162082bde640e04b83b93734d6681 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hans Bihs <hans.bihs@ntnu.no>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:08:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fnpf ice floes: horizontal lid force from the loaded surface
 gradient

The horizontal lid force on a floe is now -p*A*grad(eta) (central
differences of the stage eta) instead of p*A times the bottom tilt. It is the
exact reaction of the pressure given to the fluid (horizontal momentum
conserved), and in the edge taper it carries the side/waterline pressure of
the floe, i.e. the relative-elevation part of the mean wave drift force.

With the bottom tilt only, floe fields in waves drifted up-wave at the front
(11 of 21 floes, up to -3.4 m in 25 s, field centroid -0.1 m). Now all floes
drift down-wave (centroid +1.4 m), single floes at about the Stokes drift
(3D: 0.07 m/s vs a^2*omega*k = 0.062 m/s); static equilibrium unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tx98bAxbHpyeVhJoFooqyV
---
 src/fnpf_ice_lid.cpp | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/fnpf_ice_lid.cpp b/src/fnpf_ice_lid.cpp
index 2458aa9e4..7e5752627 100644
--- a/src/fnpf_ice_lid.cpp
+++ b/src/fnpf_ice_lid.cpp
@@ -338,10 +338,16 @@ void fnpf_ice::stage_forces(lexer *p, fdm_fnpf *c, slice &K, slice &eta)
         const double ry = e.yc - fl.x[1];
         const double rz = zb - fl.x[2];
         
-        // lid pressure normal to the tilted bottom: dF = p*A_h*nb/nb_z
-        const double nz = MAX(fl.nb[2],1.0e-6);
-        double fx = pA*fl.nb[0]/nz;
-        double fy = pA*fl.nb[1]/nz;
+        // Lid pressure on the loaded surface z = eta: dF = p*A_h*(-deta/dx, -deta/dy, 1).
+        // This is exactly the reaction of the pressure given to the fluid, so horizontal momentum is
+        // conserved. Under the rigid part eta follows the floe bottom (slope force); in the edge taper
+        // the surface gradient carries the side (waterline) pressure of the floe, which gives the
+        // relative-elevation part of the mean wave drift force. The bottom tilt alone misses it and
+        // lets floes drift up-wave in reflected wave fields.
+        const double ex = (eta(i+1,j)-eta(i-1,j))/(p->XP[IP1]-p->XP[IM1]);
+        const double ey = is2D ? 0.0 : (eta(i,j+1)-eta(i,j-1))/(p->YP[JP1]-p->YP[JM1]);
+        double fx = -pA*ex;
+        double fy = -pA*ey;
         double fz = pA;
         
         // ice-water skin drag on the relative horizontal velocity at the surface
